---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
import { article, breadcrumbs, howTo, organization } from '../../lib/seo';
import { formatUsd, regularUsd, site } from '../../data/site';
import { totalSoundCount } from '../../data/sounds';

const path = '/blog/play-a-sound-when-you-open-your-macbook';
const headline = 'How to play a sound when you open your MacBook lid';
const summary = 'macOS makes no sound when you lift the lid. Here is what it does and does not do, and how to add a lid-open sound to your Mac.';

const steps = [
  { name: 'Download and install LidShutter', text: 'Download LidShutter from lidshutter.com, open the file, and drag LidShutter into your Applications folder.' },
  { name: 'Activate your license key', text: 'Open LidShutter, open the dashboard from the menu bar icon, choose License, paste your key and press Activate.' },
  { name: 'Choose your opening sound', text: 'In the menu bar panel, pick a sound under “When I open”, or press the dice for a random one.' },
  { name: 'Choose your closing sound', text: 'Pick a goodbye sound under “When I close”. On MacBooks with a lid angle sensor it starts while the lid is still moving.' },
  { name: 'Set the volume', text: 'Use the volume slider, which goes up to 200%, and open and close your lid to hear it.' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Play a Sound When You Open Your MacBook Lid"
  description={summary}
  home={false}
  schema={[
    organization,
    article(headline, summary, path),
    howTo(headline, summary, steps),
    breadcrumbs([
      { name: 'LidShutter', path: '/' },
      { name: 'Blog', path: '/blog' },
      { name: headline, path },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <Prose eyebrow="Blog" title={headline}>
    <p>
      <strong>Short answer:</strong> your MacBook does not make a sound when you open the lid, and macOS has no setting to
      turn one on. The only sound your Mac plays on its own is the startup chime, and that is a different thing. To hear a
      sound every time you lift the lid, you need a small app such as <a href="/">LidShutter</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What macOS does and does not do</h2>
    <p>
      When you lift the lid of a MacBook that is asleep, it wakes up quietly. Nothing plays, and there is no switch in
      System Settings for a “lid open” sound.
    </p>
    <p>
      The startup chime is the sound some Macs play when they turn on from fully off. It is not tied to the lid, it does not
      play when a Mac wakes from sleep, and on many newer Macs it is off unless you turn it on. If your Mac offers it, the
      setting is in System Settings, under Sound.
    </p>

    <h2>Your options</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>An app made for it.</strong> LidShutter sits in the menu bar and plays a sound when you open the lid and
        another when you close it. It has {totalSoundCount} sounds, and you pick them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A script.</strong> If you are comfortable with scripting, tools such as Hammerspoon can run your own code
        when your Mac wakes. It takes setup, and a wake is not always the same as a lid opening.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to set it up with LidShutter</h2>
    <ol>
      {steps.map((s) => <li><strong>{s.name}.</strong> {s.text}</li>)}
    </ol>

    <h2>What it costs, and what it does not do</h2>
    <p>
      LidShutter is a one-time purchase with no subscription. One Mac costs {formatUsd(regularUsd)}, and one key can
      cover 2 to 10 Macs. It works offline after you activate it, needs {site.requirements}, and has no account and no
      analytics. See the <a href="/#pricing">pricing</a> and the <a href="/#faq">questions people ask</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/blog/macbook-lid-angle-sound">How the close sound plays before the lid shuts</a></li>
      <li><a href="/blog/sounds-made-in-code">How every LidShutter sound is made in code</a></li>
    </ul>
  </Prose>
</Base>
